{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Brings.RamificationParityMonodromy","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.constant_weight_shift_one_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.constant_weight_shift_one_residue","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L279-L285","doc":"A shift-1 operator with a nonzero zeroth-order weight reaches the residue slot\nfrom the constant term in two steps with weight `c(−2)·c(−1)`; with `c ≡ 1` that is\n`1`. So the prune is a statement about derivative-*like* operators, not about all\nof them — which is the whole point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.odd_shift_jet_monodromy_alternates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.odd_shift_jet_monodromy_alternates","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L256-L275","doc":"**The positive counterpart to `classical_jet_monodromy_constant`.** Under an\nodd-shift prolongation, a fixed-parity seed's monodromy eigenvalue alternates as\n`(−1)^n ε` along the jet tower — exactly the Door-v `(−1)^n` residual. So carrying\nthat residual requires an **odd** shift component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_anticomm_mono_of_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_anticomm_mono_of_odd","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L241-L254","doc":"**An odd shift anti-commutes with `t ↦ −t`**: it swaps the bar-even and bar-odd\nsectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_comm_mono_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_comm_mono_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L231-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.jacksonT_residue_slot_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.jacksonT_residue_slot_zero","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L222-L225","doc":"**Nor does the Jackson operator in the local coordinate**, on a power-series seed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.qddz_residue_slot_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.qddz_residue_slot_zero","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L217-L220","doc":"**q-deforming `d/dz` does not rescue the residue**, for any `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.jacksonT_annihilatesConstants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.jacksonT_annihilatesConstants","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L213-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.qddz_annihilatesConstants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.qddz_annihilatesConstants","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L209-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.jacksonT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.jacksonT","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L205-L207","doc":"The Jackson q-derivative in the local coordinate `t`: shift 1, multiplier `[e+1]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.qddz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.qddz","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L200-L203","doc":"The naive q-deformation of `d/dz`: keep shift 2, replace the multiplier\n`e + 2` by the canonical balanced q-integer `[e+2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.residue_slot_zero_shift_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.residue_slot_zero_shift_one","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L180-L192","doc":"**Shift 1.** If `c(−1) = 0` and the seed is a power series, the residue slot is\ndead at every jet level: at `n = 0, 1` the seed's own support kills it, and for\n`n ≥ 2` the `i = 1` factor is `c(−1)`. This is the Jackson operator in the local\ncoordinate and every derivative-like shift-1 operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.residue_slot_zero_shift_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.residue_slot_zero_shift_two","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L170-L178","doc":"**Shift 2.** If `c(−2) = 0` the residue slot is dead at every jet level `n ≥ 1`,\nfor **every** seed: the `i = 0` factor of the iterate product is `c(−2)`. This is\nthe classical `d/dz` and every q-deformation of its multiplier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.annihilatesConstants_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.annihilatesConstants_iff","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L157-L166","doc":"The characterisation: the operator kills the constant term iff `c(−k) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_monomial_zero_off","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_monomial_zero_off","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L152-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_monomial_zero_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_monomial_zero_apply","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L148-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.AnnihilatesConstants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.AnnihilatesConstants","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L143-L146","doc":"**Annihilating constants** is the property `c(−k) = 0`: the constant term\n`t⁰` (`monomialCoeff 0`) lands at slot `−k` with weight `c(−k)`. Every derivative\nhas it; a zeroth-order term does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.PowerSeriesSupported","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.PowerSeriesSupported","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L139-L141","doc":"A seed with no negative `t`-powers — a power series, which the colour-cubic\nbranch `X(t)` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_residue_slot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_residue_slot","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L134-L137","doc":"The residue of `X^{(n)} · 2t dt` sits at `t^{−2}`; a single shift reads it from\n`t^{k−2}` with weight `c(−2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_iterate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_iterate","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L114-L130","doc":"**The iterate**: `n` applications read the coefficient from `e + n·k` with the\nproduct of the multipliers met along the way. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_neg","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L110-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_smul","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L105-L108","doc":"Linearity in the seed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp_comp","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L97-L103","doc":"**Symbols compose**: shifts add, multipliers multiply along the shift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.ddz_eq_shiftOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.ddz_eq_shiftOp","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L93-L95","doc":"The classical prolongation `d/dz` is shift 2 with multiplier `e + 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shift2_eq_shiftOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shift2_eq_shiftOp","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L89-L91","doc":"The corpus's `shift2` is the shift-2 member. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus.shiftOp","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculus.lean#L84-L87","doc":"**Shift operator** with shift `k` and multiplier `c`: the coefficient at `tᵉ`\nis read from `t^{e+k}` with weight `c e`. The pair `(k, c)` is the operator's\nsymbol on the punctured `t`-disk. ","signatureChunk":0}]}